AB  - Root cause analysis (RCA) in microservice systems remains challenging due to heterogeneous observability signals and cascading fault propagation. We propose CausalRCA, a four-layer framework integrating: (1) multi-modal data ingestion; (2) a causal candidate graph unifying metrics, traces, logs, and topology into a temporal causal structure; (3) retrieval-augmented incident reasoning grounding LLM inference in operational knowledge; and (4) confidence-calibrated output producing top- $k$ root causes with ranked remediation actions. Evaluated on DeathStarBench with five fault types, CausalRCA achieves 86.0% top- 1 and 95.0% top-3 accuracy, outperforming the best baseline by 7.5 and 6.0 percentage points. Ablation studies confirm that the RAG module and causal graph provide complementary strengths across different fault categories.
ER  - 

