AB  - We present a federated architecture for clinical question answering (QA) that leverages retrievalaugmented generation (RAG)[4] across multiple hospital nodes without requiring centralization of sensitive patient data and incorporates Internet of Things (IoT)–based continuous patient monitoring to enhance the fidelity and timeliness. Each hospital hosts its own PostgreSQL database modeled after real-world ICU (intensive care units) datasets (MIMIC-IV, AmsterdamUMCdb, HiRID), containing either free-text notes or structured clinical data. We extract or synthesize textual representations, embed them using Sentence Transformers, and store them in local FAISS indexes. Each node exposes a semantic search API, while a central orchestrator aggregates results and passes them to a locally run LLM (LLaMA 3 via Ollama) for answer generation. Our system demonstrates the feasibility of decentralized QA over heterogeneous clinical data and paves the way for privacy-conscious, multi-center clinical decision support systems.
