AB  - Autonomous maintenance ensures reliable operation for complex intelligent infrastructure, such as power grids and communication networks. Large language models accelerate software code generation tasks. However, their probabilistic nature frequently introduces semantic errors. These specific flaws present high levels of safety risk to critical infrastructure operations. This paper proposes a neuro-symbolic architecture to resolve this issue. The framework integrates formal symbolic reasoning with neural network generation. The system transforms unstructured code modifications into organized evolution operators. A multi-stage verification pipeline enforces logical constraints on the generated code, while a safety-bounded adaptation mechanism prevents the deployment of invalid software modifications. An experimental evaluation assessed the architecture using a set of 400 software defects from power systems, IoT controllers, networks, and edge infrastructure. The final results show a verified acceptance rate of 78.2 percent. Additionally, the model preserved a safety violation rate of 0.0 percent throughout the evaluation. Formal constraints enable verifiable autonomous defect resolution for infrastructure systems.
ER  - 

