AB  - The paper presents the development of a microservice designed for intelligent categorization of user requests to an AI assistant and subsequent analysis of system usage statistics. The microservice automatically assigns one to three categories to each request, maintains a category bank considering the number of requests per category, and also forms consolidated category groups. Additionally, temporal request statistics are collected, allowing for the analysis of load dynamics and user interests across days, weeks, and months. The proposed approach can be used to improve the quality of the assistant's responses, assess interest in the AI assistant, plan resources for specific operating periods, and support management decisions.
