AB  - Modern cloud-native “systems” are distributed abstractions scattered across independent repositories. While this multi-repository, loosely-coupled approach maximizes agility, it exposes a fundamental quality assurance gap: existing CI/CD tools are confined to single-repository contexts and linear procedural execution, leaving architects with no mechanism to reason about system-wide health. Thus, cross-service architectural drift and latent security violations go undetected by design. This paper introduces the Holistic Analysis Orchestrator (HAO), a novel framework that shifts the paradigm from linear pipelines to assurance graphs. HAO's “no-code” visual wizard lets practitioners compose multi-repository verification strategies from disparate analysis engines-without scripting. We demonstrate a God's Eye workflow that ingests an entire distributed topology to concurrently perform Change Impact Analysis (CIMET), Formal Authorization Policy Consistency Verification (via SMT solvers), Neuro-Symbolic Latent Risk Assessment (Aegis), and Call-graphAware Test Suite Generation (AITest). The result is a feedbackdriven assurance fabric that unifies static analysis, formal logic, and generative validation-capabilities absent from any existing enterprise tooling.
ER  - 

